itation for case: Pruett v. Commonwealth\">232 Va. 266</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1156488\"><a href=\"/opinion/1156488/pruett-v-commonwealth/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Pruett v. Commonwealth\">351 S. E. 2d 1</a></span>; No. 86-6827, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1340635\"><a href=\"/opinion/1340635/hicks-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Hicks v. State\">256 Ga. 715</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1340635\"><a href=\"/opinion/1340635/hicks-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Hicks v. State\">352 S. E. 2d 762</a></span>; No. 86-6903, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9772433\"><a href=\"/opinion/2434166/state-v-grubbs/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Grubbs\">724 S. W. 2d 494</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9063251,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":593,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b841-14\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"ApJ\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"A1tN\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}